# Browser
# Melee, cast in the declare attackers step of its caster's turn, has its caster (Bot1), not the defending player, declare
# the blocks (CR 509.1): Bot1 has Bot2's Crimson Kobolds block Alpha Myr, where it dies, and leaves Phyrexian Walker out.
# Memnite, which nothing blocks, triggers "whenever a creature attacks and isn't blocked this combat" (CR 509.3g, 603.7):
# it is untapped and removed from combat, so it deals Bot2 no damage (CR 506.4). The pool is empty right after the cast:
# {4}{R} paid off exactly five mana. In the browser, Bot1's page shows both effects beside its life total and is asked to
# declare blockers, and clicks Bot2's creature to block.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Alpha Myr
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Melee
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Crimson Kobolds
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Alpha Myr.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Alpha Myr > Bot2; Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Melee.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Facts = Melee: You choose which creatures block this combat and how those creatures block; Melee: Whenever a creature attacks and isn't blocked this combat, untap it and remove it from combat
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Declare blockers
Bot1.Block(Crimson Kobolds > Alpha Myr)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Alpha Myr > Bot2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Crimson Kobolds
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Alpha Myr.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
